message: "If you use this software or dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "Where Does the Security Come From? A Controlled Evaluation of Context-Aware Input Sanitization Against Direct Prompt Injection"
authors:
  - family-names: Kulkarni
    given-names: Aditya
type: software
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-26"
abstract: >
  Controlled evaluation of two context-aware pre-inference sanitizers (Method A:
  hybrid hard triggers; Method B: learned fusion) against lexical baselines and
  off-the-shelf portable classifiers for direct prompt injection. Two-layer
  protocol (Bypass Rate, True ASR), dual false-positive reporting, ablations,
  and robustness on a frozen 350-prompt corpus (53-prompt test partition).
keywords:
  - prompt injection
  - direct prompt injection
  - input sanitization
  - context-aware defense
  - LLM security
